#: NAVIGATION.md:1
msgid "Single-structure and ensemble refinement with cryo-EM maps and EMMIVox"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:3
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: NAVIGATION.md:5
msgid ""
"The aim of this tutorial is to learn how to use PLUMED to perform single-"
"structure and ensemble refinement using cryo-EM maps and EMMIVox. This "
"lesson was given as part of the PLUMED masterclass series in 2022. It "
"includes:"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:8
msgid ""
"A video that explain the theory covered and a second video which shows you "
"how the exercises should be completed."
msgstr "扱う理論を解説する動画と、演習の解き方を示す2本目の動画。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:9
msgid "Two tutorials that you should try to complete yourself."
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:11
msgid "Overview of the theory"
msgstr "理論の概要"

#: NAVIGATION.md:13
msgid "The EMMIVox approach is described in the following publication:"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:15
msgid ""
"S. E. Hoff, F. E. Thomasen, K. Lindorff-Larsen, M. Bonomi. Accurate model "
"and ensemble refinement using cryo-electron microscopy maps and Bayesian "
"inference. PLoS Comput. Biol. 20 (2024) e1012180. doi: "
"[10.1371/journal.pcbi.1012180](https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1012180)."
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:18 NAVIGATION.md:63
msgid "Installation instructions"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:19
msgid ""
"Prerequisites and guide to install the software to perform EMMIVox "
"simulations can be found [here](install.md)."
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:21
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "資料"

#: NAVIGATION.md:23
msgid ""
"The data needed to complete the tutorials can be found "
"[here](https://github.com/maxbonomi/EMMIVox-Plumed-Tutorials). You can clone"
" this repository locally on your machine using the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:29
msgid "This repository contains the following 2 directories:"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:30
msgid ""
"`scripts`: python scripts used for preprocessing and analysis of EMMIVox "
"simulations"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:31
msgid ""
"`tutorials`: complete tutorials for single-structure and ensemble refinement"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:33
msgid ""
"The system under study is a Tau filament resolved at 1.9 Angstrom by the "
"Scheres group ([PDB 7P6A](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/7P6A), [EMD "
"13223](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-13223)). The system is composed by 5 "
"identical chains, for a total of 8335 solute atoms. We will simulate the "
"system using the CHARMM36m force field in explicit TIP3P water, for a total "
"of 40958 atoms. The reference is:"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:37
msgid ""
"[Shi, Y., Zhang, W., Yang, Y. et al. Structure-based classification of "
"tauopathies. Nature 598, 359–363 "
"(2021)](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-03911-7)"
msgstr ""

